Foundational Technical Skills

These are essential regardless of whether you’re in SAP or any other skills (Apart from Cloud/Devops) moving into AI/DevOps.

------> Programming Skills

Python – Most common for AI/ML and automation

Bonus: Shell scripting or basic Bash if you're doing DevOps work


----->Operating Systems

Linux basics – Command-line, file system, permissions

Why: Most DevOps tools and AI workloads run on Linux

2. Basic AI/ML Concepts

Even if you’re not building models, understanding these will help you use AI tools effectively.

Machine Learning (ML): Supervised vs unsupervised learning, models, training/testing

Deep Learning (optional but helpful): Neural networks, TensorFlow, or PyTorch (basic level)

Data Preparation: Cleaning, feature engineering, etc.

You can take an intro course on Coursera, Udemy, or freeCodeCamp to get started.

3. DevOps Basics

If you're newer to DevOps, focus on these core areas:

CI/CD – Tools like Jenkins, GitLab CI, or GitHub Actions

Containers – Docker and Kubernetes basics

Infrastructure as Code (IaC) – Terraform or Ansible

Monitoring/Logging – Prometheus, Grafana, ELK stack

4. AI for DevOps (AIOps) Specific Topics

This is where AI meets DevOps. Learn:

Anomaly detection for system performance and logs

Predictive analytics for capacity planning

ChatOps – Using AI/ML in tools like Slack, MS Teams with bots

Log analysis using AI (e.g., Logz.io, Datadog, Splunk with ML add-ons)
